198
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:16,200
This phrase, without further ado, is something that we commonly hear in speeches or more formal occasions, but it's something that we say when we want to introduce something.

199
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,940
We say, we're not going to talk about it anymore.

200
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:18,940
Let's just do it.

201
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:19,700
Let's just show you.

202
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:24,340
So the word ado, is this, this is I think like classic English.

203
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,220
It's not really common to hear it anymore.

204
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:31,520
No, there is actually a very famous play by Shakespeare called Much Ado About Nothing.

205
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:38,480
And that means, you know, that there's a lot of talking and a lot of problems and a lot of drama about this one thing.

206
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:46,240
And so basically when we say the phrase without further ado, we're saying, you know, without further talking, talking about this anymore.

207
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,240
Yeah.

208
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,240
Okay.

209
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:53,100
So it's a nice way to say, okay, finally we're going to do this, or finally we're going to see this.

